.Language=English,English
.PluginContents=Rename files (NewName)

@Contents
$^#Rename files#

    This plugin module allows to rename files with regular expressions usage.
It works only in Far 1.70 build 1634 and above. Some useful information is
absent in this help, but you can find it in standard documentation of
~Search and Replace (S&R)~@<..\..\>@ plug-in.

     Process of renaming is almost the same as
search and replace, but in this case not file contents, but
file #name# is processed. If you still don't understand what a unique
thing you've got, look at ~the examples~@RenameExamples@.

     Attention: #files descriptions are not updated# in the current version!

^#Dialog description:#

     Major part of options and buttons are similar to the same-named ones of
~S&R~@<..\..\>MainDialog@ plug-in.

     If #selected# processing is being performed and option
#Process subfolders# is turned off, mere folders will be renamed as
if they were files.

 #Search#       ~Regular expression~@<..\..\>RegExp@, which specifies search string for
              #processed files names#. Notice that you may have to
              enclose search string in slashes depending on
              ~settings of S&R~@<..\..\>CfgSearch@.

 #Replace with# Replacement string ~regular expression~@<..\..\>ReplaceRegExp@.

 #Initiate#     Affects #\### ~regexp~@<..\..\>ReplaceRegExp@.
 #value of the#
 #counter by#
 #zero in each#
 #directory#

 #Write#        Plug-in will create a file with information about
 #log-file#     renaming process. You can tune up format of log-name
              and format of log-contents in ~configuration~@Config@
              Log-file will have a name YYYY_MM_DD_hh_mm_cc.bat by
              default, it may be used to rollback performed name
              changes at any time. #Remark:# log is created only
              after main job is done, because records must be
              placed in log in reverse order.

 #Confirmation# If option is set renaming confirmation dialog will
 #of the#       be shown. You can change new filename in this dialog.
 #renaming#

 #Scheme#       Call schemes manipulations menu.
              Use #Alt-Shift-0#...#Alt-Shift-9# for quick switching
              between first 10 schemes.

 #Save#         Save current settings as a scheme
              (you'll be prompted for a scheme name).

 See file #Reg\newnamescheme.reg# for additional examples.

 ~Contents~@Contents@
@RenameExamples
$^#Examples of settings for files renaming#

    All the examples are divided into two groups. Examples do now show
all the possible variants of #newname.srp# usage, but they are made
for those persons, who moved to this 2nd level plug-in from my another plug-in
NewName, and for those, who have removed standard #Case conversion# plug-in,
which is distributed with ~FAR~@:Contents@.

^#NewName.dll replacement#

    The correspondences between special sequences of
newname.dll and S&R regexps are listed below:

  #File order#       See description of ~\##~@<..\..\>ReplaceRegExp@
  #number#

  #Total number of#  No equivalent, you'll have to specify
  #processed files#  the number actually.

  #Filename with#    ~$0~@<..\..\>ReplaceRegExp@
  #extension#

  #Filename without extension#, #Extension#
    If search string looks like "#^(.+)\.(.*)$#", then
~$1~@<..\..\>ReplaceRegExp@ stands for filename, and
~$2~@<..\..\>ReplaceRegExp@ for extension.


^#FileCase.dll replacement#

     Correspondence for some file case conversion types.

      Type      |   Search string    | Replacement String
  --------------------------------------------------------
  #Filename.ext#  | ^(.)(.*)$          | \u$1\L$2
  #Filename.Ext#  | ^(.)(.*)\.(.)(.*)$ | \u$1\L$2.\u$3\L$4
  #filename.ext#  | ^.+$               | \L$0
  #FILENAME.EXT#  | ^.+$               | \U$0
  #File Name.Ext# | ((\w)([^\s\.]*))+  | \u$2\L$3

 ~Contents~@Contents@
@Config
$^#NewName: configuration#

^#History#

  You can specify which history is to be used in NewName dialog for the following
fields: "#Search for#", "#Replace with#".

  #History of S&R#    Use #S&R# history settings.
  #Another history#   You may set registry keys names to store
                    history.

^#Log#

    Don't change this settings if you don't understand what you want to do!

    #Template: Log-filename#
    ~Regular expression for replace string~@<..\..\>ReplaceRegExp@. Using
this template NewName will build the name of a log-file. You can use
any regexp operators except operators which are working only with
~processing of files group~@<..\..\>ReplaceRegExp@ (exception -
~\P~@<..\..\>ReplaceRegExp@ operator) in this template.

    #Template: successful and unsuccessful renaming#
    ~Regular expression for replace string~@<..\..\>ReplaceRegExp@. Using
this template NewName will build log-records. Note that
~$0~@<..\..\>ReplaceRegExp@ operator means new name of file with path,
~$1~@<..\..\>ReplaceRegExp@ means new name of file without path, and operators
which are working only with
~processing of files group~@<..\..\>ReplaceRegExp@ use old filename
information.

 ~Contents~@Contents@
